  "name": "Pagination cursor",
  "definition": "An opaque continuation token for the next page of one query. It binds the operation, normalized filter key, query snapshot, and next offset; malformed or reused tokens are rejected, and a changed snapshot returns a retryable stale-snapshot error. Its checksum detects corruption but is not an authorization credential.",
